      "message": "fix(3d): a whole-model 3D Pocket clears an open-sided notch past its edge\n\nThe 3D Pocket's footprint was the model's silhouette, and the level law\nerodes it by the tool radius, so the cutter's edge never passed the\nsilhouette. A notch open to the part's outside kept a band one radius\nwide, the full stock height tall, along its open edges, and the op read\nok; the next setup's fixture check then refused the post.\n\nThe source-built footprint of an untilted whole-model 3D Pocket (and of\nMulti-Axis Rough, its stamped twin) now grows past the silhouette by the\ntool radius less 0.01 mm (machining3d::open_sides), minus the setup's\nother parts. The centre rides up to the silhouette edge where a level is\nopen; where a level's material is flush with the silhouette the band is\nnarrower than the erosion and cuts nothing. A picked or Boundary-\ncontrolled region and a tilted plane keep the old reading.\n\nBoth kinds now read the setup's other parts in the solid law\n(keep_law::neighbour_parts) as a second net, which also names a cut\nthrough a part standing inside the model's own silhouette.\n\nThe #1706 pin on the as-imported sample (no tool fit inside a 6.53 mm\nstrip, so the op refused) now pins that the pocket clears beside the\nstrip and verifies clean.\n\nFixes #1749\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
